## Fernhill's claims: what the finished story can reach and what it can never
## reach, each under the rooms, things and verbs that are load-bearing on the
## way. The test tree's manifest names this file; the story never imports it.
## The shared set is the winning line (WALKTHROUGH.txt); a claim that needs
## less declares its own.

claims
  needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Boiler Shed, the Entrance Hall, the Kitchen, the Greenhouse, the Folly Hill, the Folly
  needs things: Tobias, the stopcock, the primer plunger, the boiler, the garden shears, the sherry bottle, Mrs Kettle, the vine, the silver locket, the folly door, the fuse, the deed box, the deed
  needs verbs: ask, turn, push, switch on, turn on, take, give, prune, open, cut

  claim the story can be won
    the story ends in victory

  claim the deed is in hand
    the player has the deed

  claim Tobias has been asked about the folly
    Tobias was asked about "the folly"
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive
    needs things: Tobias
    needs verbs: ask

  claim the diary page has been read
    the diary page is read
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Entrance Hall, the Kitchen, the Study
    needs things: the sherry bottle, Mrs Kettle, the travelling trunk, the diary page
    needs verbs: take, give, open, read

  never the deed box leaves the Folly
    the deed box is not in the Folly
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Boiler Shed, the Greenhouse, the Folly Hill, the Folly
    needs things: Tobias, the stopcock, the primer plunger, the boiler, the folly door, the deed box
    needs verbs: ask, turn, push, turn on, open, take

  claim the Study is reached
    the player is in the Study
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Entrance Hall, the Kitchen, the Study
    needs things: the sherry bottle, Mrs Kettle
    needs verbs: take, give

  never the Study is reached without the sherry
    the player is in the Study
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Entrance Hall, the Kitchen, the Study
    needs things: the garden shears, Mrs Kettle
    needs verbs: take, give

  claim the auction notice has been read
    the auction notice is read
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates
    needs things: the auction notice
    needs verbs: read

  claim the stopcock has been turned
    the stopcock has been turned
    needs rooms: the Iron Gates, the Gravel Drive, the Fountain Court, the Boiler Shed
    needs things: the stopcock
    needs verbs: turn
end claims
